// vkernels/kernels/dsa.cu -- CUDA wmma implementation (NVIDIA), a port of
// the gfx942 MFMA top-k logits kernel in dsa.hip (issue #51) for an NVIDIA
// deployment track (verified on GB10 / Grace-Blackwell, sm_121).
//
//   out[b, t] = k_scale[ page[b,i], j ]
//             * Sum_h ( max(0, Sum_d Q[b,h,d] * K[ page[b,i], j,d ] )
//                       * gate[b, h] )
//   where t = i*B + j, t < seq_len[b] (else left unwritten). See dsa.hpp
//   for the full gated-logit formula and the tensor layout.
//
// Three device variants mirror dsa.hip exactly:
//   * dsa_topk_logits_kernel        -- fp32-Q scalar (Q dequanted once)
//   * dsa_topk_logits_kernel_fp8q   -- fp8-Q  scalar (Q raw, dequant OTF)
//   * dsa_topk_logits_kernel_mfma   -- bf16 wmma Matrix-Core (FAST path)
//
// The two scalar kernels are near-verbatim translations of the HIP originals
// (one warp per (batch, split_kv) block, one lane per KV token, sequential
